    <DataNode elementId="AT5G44630-MONOMER" textLabel="AT5G44630-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q4KSH9" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="495" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The terpene synthase coded by AT5G44630 in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; produces a large number of volatile sesquiterpenes from farnesyl diphosphate. The variety of products can be accounted for by rearrangements in unstable intermediates|CITS: [15918888]|. The major products are (+)-&amp;alpha;-barbatene and (+)-thujopsene, while 11 other identified compounds and a number of unidentified compounds are also produced|CITS: [15918888]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G44630-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G44630.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q4KSH9" />
